%N A399332 The binomial matrix of the Euler up/down numbers, square array read by ascending antidiagonals.
%C A399332 See the comments and links in A399000.
%H A399332 Peter Luschny, <a href="https://github.com/PeterLuschny/Gists/blob/main/GnomonicExpansionAndBinomialMatrices.ipynb">Gnomonic Expansion and Binomial Matrices</a>, a Python notebook.
%F A399332 A(n, n) = E(n) := 2^n*abs(Euler(n, 1/2) + Euler(n, 1)) if n > 0, E(0) = 1.
%F A399332 A(n, k) = Sum_{m=0..d} binomial(d, m) * s^(d - m) * E(p + m), where d = abs(n - k), p = min(n, k), s = 1 if k <= n, otherwise -1.
